{"id":"r6","level":1,"levelName":"Reading","n":6,"of":9,"title":"Vowels: a and e","titleHe":"נִקּוּד: a וְ־e","goal":"Read the four marks that make the a and e sounds.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Vowels are marks written under (mostly) the consonant they follow. So בַ is read ba, not ab — consonant first, then its vowel. Modern Hebrew has fewer vowel sounds than it has marks, so several marks share a sound."},{"type":"vowels","ids":["ַ","ָ","ֵ","ֶ"],"items":[{"sign":"ַ","on":"בַ","name":"פַּתַח","en":"patach","sound":"a as in father"},{"sign":"ָ","on":"בָ","name":"קָמַץ","en":"kamatz","sound":"a as in father"},{"sign":"ֵ","on":"בֵ","name":"צֵירֵי","en":"tsere","sound":"e as in they"},{"sign":"ֶ","on":"בֶ","name":"סֶגוֹל","en":"segol","sound":"e as in bed"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"פַּתַח and קָמַץ both say a. צֵירֵי and סֶגוֹל both say e. They look different and are spelled differently, but you pronounce each pair the same."}],"vocab":[{"he":"דָּג","en":"fish","translit":"dag"},{"he":"יָם","en":"sea","translit":"yam"},{"he":"אֵם","en":"mother","translit":"em"},{"he":"בֵּן","en":"son","translit":"ben"},{"he":"דֶּלֶת","en":"door","translit":"delet"},{"he":"עֶרֶב","en":"evening","translit":"erev"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["a as in father","e as in bed","i as in machine","e as in they"],"correct":0,"prompt":"בַ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["i as in machine","e as in bed","e as in they","a as in father"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בָ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["e as in bed","a as in father","a as in father","e as in they"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בֵ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["e as in bed","a as in father","e as in they","a as in father"],"correct":0,"prompt":"בֶ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["root","brother","longing","fish"],"correct":3,"prompt":"דָּג","translit":"dag"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["enjoy the new one","sea","night","there isn't"],"correct":1,"prompt":"יָם","translit":"yam"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["mother","eye","length","orange"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אֵם","translit":"em"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “door”?","options":["אֵיךְ קוֹרְאִים לְךָ","כָּל כָּךְ","בָּרִיא","דֶּלֶת"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"דָּג","translit":"dag","en":"fish"},{"type":"choice","q":"Which mark is segol?","options":["בַ","בֶ","בֵ","בָ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"דֶּלֶת","translit":"delet","en":"door"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “son”?","options":["בֵּן","עֲלִיָּה","חֹפֶשׁ","בַּת"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “sea”?","options":["חֻלְצָה","בֶּאֱמֶת","אָמַר","יָם"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["דֶּלֶת","בֵּן","אֵם","עֶרֶב"],"correct":2,"say":"אֵם","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “fish”?","options":["דָּג","תְּנוּעָה","נֶפֶשׁ","עֲבוֹדָה"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “mother” in Hebrew","answer":"אֵם","hint":"em"}]}